# BNS AWS Terraform -- shell environment template
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The Makefile sources this file, so it only needs values that are used by
# the AWS CLI / helper scripts. Terraform inputs live in the per-stack
# terraform.tfvars files instead.

# ============================================================
# AWS credentials
# ============================================================
# Named profile from ~/.aws/credentials or ~/.aws/config.
# Using a profile keeps long-lived keys out of the shell environment.
# The profile that assumes the operator role. It needs role_arn, mfa_serial
# and source_profile in ~/.aws/config -- `make output-bootstrap` prints a
# ready-to-paste block.
#
# Terraform cannot prompt for an MFA token, so a session has to be in the
# environment before any target that talks to AWS:
#
#   eval "$(make login)"
#
# That sets AWS_SESSION_TOKEN, and the Makefile then stops exporting this
# variable so the session is not overridden by it.
AWS_PROFILE=bns

# Region the foundation stack is deployed into.
# Fixed once and for all: ECR images and S3 objects are region-bound, so
# moving later means re-pushing the ~4 GB image. Run `make region-scout`
# before deciding.
AWS_REGION=us-west-2

# ============================================================
# Region scouting
# ============================================================
# Candidate regions compared by scripts/region_scout.sh.
SCOUT_REGIONS="us-east-1 us-east-2 us-west-2"

# Instance types to score. The first entry is the production target.
#
# The gallery BNS is a small grid -- about 8.3 M points on a quarter domain,
# 43.8 GByte from Carpet and ~89 GiB resident over 32 ranks in the gallery's
# own run -- so the question is not which 48xlarge fits but which smaller
# size gives the best price per useful core-hour. None of it is measured on
# this project yet; the throughput probe decides.
#
# c7a.24xlarge  AMD Genoa, 96 physical cores (SMT off), 192 GiB. Twice the
#               gallery run's footprint. 24 ranks x 4 threads is the
#               gallery's Frontera shape.
# c7a.16xlarge  64 cores, 128 GiB. Fits, more tightly, and the calmest spot
#               pool of the family in us-west-2 (Spot Advisor 2026-09-13:
#               5-10% interruption against >20% for the 24xlarge).
# c7a.48xlarge  192 cores, 384 GiB. The GW230529 production type; the best
#               price per physical core, but at 192 ranks this grid would be
#               ghost-zone dominated. Scored as the fallback, not the target.
#
# c7i is not an equivalent: hyperthreads on half as many physical cores, on
# 8 memory channels rather than 12, about 2x the cost per physical
# core-hour for a bandwidth-bound evolution.
SCOUT_INSTANCE_TYPES="c7a.24xlarge c7a.16xlarge c7a.48xlarge"

# Target capacity in vCPUs used for the spot placement score query.
SCOUT_TARGET_VCPUS=96

# ============================================================
# Terraform plugin cache
# ============================================================
# Shared provider download directory. The AWS provider is around 840 MB and
# all three stacks use it, so without a shared cache the checkout triples.
# The Makefile sets this automatically; override it here if the home
# directory is on slow storage.
# TF_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR=${HOME}/.terraform.d/plugin-cache
